---
import { ISSUES_URL } from '../config'
import Document from '../layouts/Document.astro'

const services = [
  {
    name: 'YouTube',
    url: 'https://www.youtube.com',
    use: 'YouTube Music and YouTube: search, song and video details, audio and radio.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Spotify',
    url: 'https://www.spotify.com',
    use: 'Only if you switch the integration on: search, related artists and song radio. If you connect your Spotify account, also your recommendations, liked songs and playlists.',
  },
  { name: 'LRCLIB', url: 'https://lrclib.net', use: 'Synced lyrics.' },
  {
    name: 'MusicBrainz',
    url: 'https://musicbrainz.org',
    use: 'Song, album and artist information.',
  },
  {
    name: 'ListenBrainz',
    url: 'https://listenbrainz.org',
    use: 'Recommendations for your home feed.',
  },
  { name: 'Last.fm', url: 'https://www.last.fm', use: 'Recommendations for your home feed.' },
  {
    name: 'Internet Archive',
    url: 'https://archive.org',
    use: 'Free music, including lossless FLAC.',
  },
  { name: 'Jamendo', url: 'https://www.jamendo.com', use: 'Free music, including lossless FLAC.' },
]
---

<Document
  title="Privacy · FXM"
  description="FXM has no analytics, no accounts and no servers, and sets no cookies. Your data stays on your device. Here is which services your device talks to, and why."
  heading="Privacy"
  lead="FXM is built so that there is nothing to collect: no analytics, no accounts, no cookies set by FXM, and your data stays on your device."
  updated="2026-10-25"
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No analytics or tracking.</strong>
      This website and the FXM apps contain no analytics, trackers or ad scripts.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No accounts.</strong>
      There is nothing to sign up for, so FXM never has your name, email address or password.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No cookies set by FXM.</strong>
      FXM doesn't use cookies. Services you sign in to, such as Spotify, may set their own.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No FXM servers.</strong>
      Searches and plays don't pass through FXM, so FXM can't see what you look for or listen to.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
  <p>
    Your library (likes and playlists), listening history, settings and downloads are stored on your
    device: in your browser's storage for the web app, or in the app's own storage on desktop and
    Android. FXM can't see them.
  </p>
  <p>Clearing this site's data in your browser, or uninstalling the app, deletes them for good.</p>

  <h2>Services your device talks to</h2>
  <p>
    FXM gets music, information and lyrics straight from the services below. Your device connects to
    them directly; in the web app, some of these requests go through the FXM Connect extension in
    your browser. As with any website you visit, they receive your IP address and the requests made
    for you, such as a search or the song you're playing, and their own privacy policies apply.
  </p>
  <dl class="services">
    {services.map((service) => (
      <div>
        <dt>
          <a href={service.url}>{service.name}</a>
        </dt>
        <dd>{service.use}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2>This website and app downloads</h2>
  <p>
    This website and the web app are static files hosted on Cloudflare Pages, and app downloads are
    published on GitHub Releases. Like any host, Cloudflare and GitHub handle the network requests
    needed to deliver those files, under their own privacy policies. FXM doesn't add analytics or
    tracking to either.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If the way FXM handles data ever changes, this page will be updated and the date at the top will
    change.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>Ask on the <a href={ISSUES_URL}>FXM issue tracker on GitHub</a>.</p>
</Document>

<style>
.services {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--space-2);
  margin-top: var(--space-5);
}

.services div {
  display: grid;
  gap: var(--space-1);
  padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
  border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  background: var(--color-surface);
}

.services dt {
  font-weight: 700;
}

.services dd {
  color: var(--color-text-muted);
}

@media (min-width: 40rem) {
  .services div {
    grid-template-columns: 10rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
}
</style>
